<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet>
  <title>Differential Equations</title>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that <m>P(t)</m> describes the population of a particular
  species, where <m>P</m> is represented in millions.  Suppose also that
  the change in the population is determined by the differential
  equation
  <md>
  \frac{dP}{dt}=f(P)
  </md>
  where <m>f(P)</m> is the function graphed below.</p>
        <p><image source="figures/30-threshold.png"/></p>
        <p>For what values of the population <m>P</m> does the population increase?
  For what values of the population <m>P</m> does the population decrease?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Identify any equilibrium populations.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1.5in">
      <statement>
        <p>Sketch a slope field for the differential equation <m>\frac{dP}{dt} =
  f(P)</m>.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Determine whether the equilibrium populations you have found are
  either stable or unstable.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>If <m>P(0)&lt;1</m>, what happens to this species eventually?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>If <m>P(0)&gt;1</m>, what happens eventually?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that <m>P(t)</m> describes the population of a particular
  species of fish in a lake where <m>P</m> is measured in thousands and <m>t</m>
  is measured in months.  Suppose that the change in the population is
  given by the differential equation
  <md>
  \frac{dP}{dt} = P(6-P).
  </md></p>
        <p>Sketch a graph of the function <m>f(P) = P(6-P)</m> and use it to
  determine any equilibrium solutions.</p>
        <p>Determine whether these equilibria are stable or unstable.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>What happens to the population of fish eventually?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Suppose that the lake is opened to fishing and that one thousand
  fish per month are removed from the lake (remember that <m>P</m> is
  measured in <em>thousands</em> of fish).  Modify the differential
  equation to take this into account.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>Determine the new equilibrium solutions and their stability.</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1in">
      <statement>
        <p>What happens to the fish after a long time?</p>
      </statement>
    </task>
  </exercise>

</worksheet>
